the music's bars. Each shot is played and recorded on its own by Godot's movie writer, through
scenes/dev/trailer.tscn for play and scenes/dev/trailer_posed.tscn for the posed screens, at a
fixed frame rate so it plays the same every time. ffmpeg cuts them together in order, frame for
frame, a few with a transition laid across the cut, and lays the music under them: Ovani Sound's
Deceased Rodent, its beats on the trailer's half seconds, its calm layer muffled under the opening,
its tense one on the drop for a bar settling into the calm one, going up to its tense layer and
then its peak at the trailer's turns, and back to the calm one muffled under the license at the
end; the game's own sound quieter beneath it.

A draft is drawn at 1920x1080; the final, `--final`, at 3840x2160 and scaled down to 1920x1080 for
smooth edges, as the store's screenshots are; and `--8k` at 7680x4320, scaled down to two at once:
3840x2160 for YouTube and 1920x1080 for the store.

Usage: tools/trailer [--final|--8k] [shot ...]   renders the shots named, or all, then cuts the
                                                 trailer
       tools/trailer [--final|--8k] --cut        only cuts the trailer, from the shots recorded
       GODOT_HIDDEN=1 tools/trailer              renders without a window, in gamescope
       JOBS=3 tools/trailer                      renders this many shots at once (default 3, at 8K
                                                 1; more crash the hidden display now and then)
Writes build/trailer/jackpot-junction-trailer.mp4, -draft.mp4 or -4k.mp4, and each shot's recording
to build/trailer/shots, shots-draft or shots-8k, which a later run cutting only some shots again
reuses.
"""

